        {
          "kicker": "Coaching change",
          "heading": "Fiji Rugby parted ways with Mick Byrne in April by mutual agreement",
          "body": "In April, Fiji Rugby and Mick Byrne parted ways \"by mutual agreement\", leaving the Flying Fijians looking for a new coach 18 months before the Rugby World Cup. Byrne had been in charge since 2024, after a spell at Fijian Drua, and his tenure brought wins over Scotland, Wales and Japan. AFP reported he appeared to have a difference of opinion with management over future plans. Byrne said he had been honoured to work with the Flying Fijians players and staff."
        },
