      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Squad selection",
          "heading": "Galthié's France went to Christchurch without its biggest stars, Dupont included",
          "body": "Ahead of the July Nations Championship opener against New Zealand, coverage from early July reported that Fabien Galthié's touring squad left out Antoine Dupont, Romain Ntamack, Thomas Ramos, Grégory Alldritt and Louis Bielle-Biarrey. Many of the absences were tied to player workload after the long Top 14 season, leaving France to lean on a younger group against one of the toughest road opponents in international rugby."
        },
