      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Rankings threat",
          "heading": "Wallabies cling to sixth in world rankings after All Blacks loss",
          "body": "Eden Park cost the Wallabies more than a 50-19 scoreline: their World Rugby rating slipped from 85.55 to 84.89, leaving them sixth and just 0.11 ahead of Scotland in seventh. Had they won by more than 15 points, they could have moved into fourth, their highest ranking since November 2021, but that opportunity is gone. Another defeat in next Saturday's Sydney rematch would see them slip behind the Scots."
        },
