          "heading": "Hajime Shoji's League One reverses plan to treat naturalised players as foreign",
          "body": "In late August, Japan Rugby League One, the domestic club competition, has backed down on registration rules that would have classed some Japanese-passport holders as foreign. Players who acquired Japanese citizenship, or applied, by May 2025 will now be treated as Japanese-born under the 2026-27 system, which begins in December. The original plan would have limited places for foreign-born players eligible to represent Japan. Shoji admitted: \"We lacked communication with players who would be adversely affected by the changes.\""
