          "body": "In World Rugby's men's rankings, New Zealand rose 0.66 to 91.81 after the 31-point Eden Park win over Australia, 1.28 behind the Springboks on 93.09. The gap stood at almost four points after the Springboks beat the Wallabies 3-1 in Rugby's Greatest Rivalry, and Australia stayed sixth on 84.89. Providing they get through next week's Sydney Test unscathed, Planet Rugby says the All Blacks may fancy finishing the year as the top-ranked side."
